The LZMA SDK's 7z decoder, from 7-Zip 26.02's C/ (Igor Pavlov; public domain, as each file's header says), the part
that unpacks a file of a .7z into memory: the archive's reader (7zArcIn.c, 7zDec.c, 7zBuf.c, 7zStream.c, 7zAlloc.c),
its CRC (7zCrc.c, 7zCrcOpt.c), LZMA and LZMA2 (LzmaDec.c, Lzma2Dec.c), the branch and Delta filters (Bcj2.c, Bra.c,
Bra86.c, BraIA64.c, Delta.c), CpuArch.c, and the headers they include. Unchanged.

  source   https://github.com/ip7z/7zip
  tag      26.02, commit f9d78aff31a5f2521ae7ddbdc97c4a8855808959 (26 Jun 2026)
  files    as SHA256SUMS lists them, each the tag's C/ file (sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS in this folder; kiwami/tests/ci.sh runs it)

Left out: PPMd (7zDec.c builds without it unless Z7_PPMD_SUPPORT is defined, which kiwami.mk doesn't), the encoders,
AES, and the Windows-only headers (7zWindows.h, included only under _WIN32). libchdr bundles the same version's
LzmaDec.c with its symbols renamed (../libchdr/deps/lzma-26.02), built beside this one. Built into banana-ui by
ui/src/kiwami/kiwami.mk, used by ui/src/kiwami/ra7z.cpp. A bump copies the same files from the new tag's C/, writes
SHA256SUMS again from them, and checks kiwami/DEPENDENCIES.md's notes.
